stdout. `gh auth token` is the common human-friendly helper, but any secret manager command can be used.\"}],[\"/sources/jira\",{\"id\":\"/sources/jira\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/jira\",\"type\":\"page\",\"content\":\"Jira source\",\"breadcrumbs\":[\"AgentBoard\",\"Sources\"],\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/sources/jira\"}],[\"/sources/jira-0\",{\"id\":\"/sources/jira-0\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/jira\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/sources/jira#jira-source\",\"content\":\"Jira source\"}],[\"/sources/jira-1\",{\"id\":\"/sources/jira-1\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/jira\",\"type\":\"heading\",\"tags\":[],\"url\":\"/sources/jira#field-mapping\",\"content\":\"Field mapping\"}],[\"/sources/jira-2\",{\"id\":\"/sources/jira-2\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/jira\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/jira#jira-source\",\"content\":\"Use `kind = \\\"jira\\\"` to collect Jira issues with JQL.\"}],[\"/sources/jira-3\",{\"id\":\"/sources/jira-3\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/jira\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/jira#jira-source\",\"content\":\"Credentials come from environment variables by default. Defaults are `JIRA_EMAIL`\\nand `JIRA_API_TOKEN`.\"}],[\"/sources/jira-4\",{\"id\":\"/sources/jira-4\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/jira\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/jira#jira-source\",\"content\":\"Or configure a credential helper. AgentBoard writes Git-style request lines to\\nstdin (`protocol`, `host`) and reads either `username`/`password` or\\n`email`/`token` lines from stdout.\"}],[\"/sources/jira-5\",{\"id\":\"/sources/jira-5\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/jira\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/jira#field-mapping\",\"content\":\"AgentBoard uses Jira's internal issue `id` as stable `item.id` inside the Jira\\nsite's Item Store. The Jira issue key is the default `item.reference_id`.\"}],[\"/sources/jira-6\",{\"id\":\"/sources/jira-6\",\"page_id\":\"/sources/jira\",\"tags\":[],\"type\":\"text\",\"url\":\"/sources/jira#field-mapping\",\"c